{
 "title": "Meridian Service Portal containers",
 "description": "The portal API stores receipts and outbox records in one transaction and reads ERP facts from a versioned read model. A handoff worker delivers submissions to the CRM, and the CRM sends case status updates back to the portal API, which projects them for customers. When the CRM approves a case it emits ServiceCaseApproved; the work-order integration consumes it and creates the ERP work order. A sync job refreshes the ERP read model through ERP's read API. Everything inside the Meridian solution boundary is run by the portal team. Solid arrows are synchronous calls or writes; dashed arrows are asynchronous events or status updates.",
